 "verdict": "NO MATERIAL DIFFERENCE - hypothesis H023 DESTROYED",
 "interpretation": [
  "The tuning-set signal did not replicate out-of-sample. At k=1500, where the tuning evidence was strongest (rho=-0.189, p=0.0041), the out-of-sample paired test is null (p=0.70) and the candidate WINS ONLY 48% of epochs while showing a lower mean MAE - i.e. the -3.31% headline is carried by a few large residuals, not by consistent improvement.",
  "At k=500 and k=1000 the candidate is WORSE than the champion out-of-sample.",
  "Ridge shrinkage bought nothing: the tuning curve is nearly flat in alpha and the selected alpha was 0.0 at two horizons. With only 2-3 features, OLS at n=60 is not meaningfully over-fitting, so there was no variance for the penalty to remove.",
  "This is the pre-registered failure mode of tuning-set selection, and the protocol caught it. Had alpha and the feature set been chosen on the test epochs, k=1500 would have been reported as a 3.3% improvement."
 ],
 "conclusion": "Within-epoch pace trend is not exploitable from headers alone. This closes the last untested representation idea on the existing feature set and corroborates remaining_information_gap.json: the residual is a NEW-INFORMATION problem, not a representation or model-complexity problem.",
